WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.839
In this video, we'll show you how to

2
00:00:02.879 --> 00:00:08.639
install Tessle onto your machine. You

3
00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:11.360
will need to download the Tessle CLI,

4
00:00:08.639 --> 00:00:14.960
which can be done using MPM. You'll need

5
00:00:11.360 --> 00:00:19.119
a node version 22 or higher.

6
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:22.160
At a terminal, run npm install-g

7
00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:24.320
passing in the URL shown. You can test

8
00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:26.800
the CLI installation by running the

9
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:28.960
command tessle-help to check that

10
00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:30.800
everything is working.

11
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:32.880
Once your installation is complete, you

12
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:35.440
can authenticate with Tessle by running

13
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:37.520
Tessle login.

14
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:40.000
This will redirect you to a browser for

15
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:42.719
you to authenticate and confirm the code

16
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.800
from your terminal.

17
00:00:42.719 --> 00:00:46.640
Upon confirmation, you may close the

18
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.480
browser tab and your terminal will

19
00:00:46.640 --> 00:00:50.800
notify you that your login was

20
00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:52.239
successful.

21
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.320
You can test whether you are

22
00:00:52.239 --> 00:00:56.879
authenticated at any time by running

23
00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:58.800
Tessle. Who am I?

24
00:00:56.879 --> 00:01:01.680
You should now have an authenticated

25
00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:06.000
Tessle installation. Your next step is

26
00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:06.000
to initialize Tessle in a project.
